.TH ARES_SET_SOCKET_CLOSE_CALLBACK 3 "10 September 2026"
.SH NAME
ares_set_socket_close_callback \- replace socket closing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ares.h>

void ares_set_socket_close_callback(ares_channel_t *channel,
                                   ares_sock_close_callback callback,
                                   void *user_data);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs a callback that takes ownership of each socket when c-ares is finished
using it. The callback must close the socket, but may defer that close until
an external event loop has acknowledged deregistration. c-ares does not use
or close the socket after invoking the callback.
.PP
A NULL callback restores closing through the channel's socket functions.
The setting is copied by ares_dup. The callback must not retain the channel:
it may run during ares_destroy. The application owns the lifetime of user_data.
.PP
The setting cannot be used with ARES_OPT_EVENT_THREAD and is ignored for those
channels. Configure it before starting queries.
.SH SEE ALSO
ares_set_socket_functions_ex(3), ares_destroy(3)
